WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.620 --> 00:00:08.019 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  [Music]  a couple of weekends ago i was playing  through the third and final title update  15 pts i missed the second one so i was  wanting to see some of the changes that  had been implemented for the countdown  game mode but also wanted to try out  some of the new gear  the devs had announced that there were  some issues with some of the pieces that  were causing some disconnects and deltas  so these have been removed but given  that i was having nothing but delta  issues unable to even finish a single  countdown session i thought i'd have a  bit of a muck around with them anyway  i've seen the hundreds of videos coming  out about the pts builds weapons and  every small change and tweet coming from  the developers so don't worry this won't  just be another one of those  this video will be a little bit  different i'm actually not quite sure  what to make of it to be honest and i'm  hoping you may be able to help some of  you may remember seeing a video i put  out a while ago called named and exotic  items story slash law  this was a summary of a number of items  available in-game that had a bit of  background and story that most people  would overlook when playing through for  example the white death named marksman  rifle pays homage to simu hayaha a  finnish military sniper in the winter  war who was believed to have killed over  500 men he went on to live up until the  ripe old age of 96 despite having half  his face blown off by a red army  explosive round  i'll chuck that video in the top right  corner if you wanted to check it out  so this will be a video similar to that  where i will go over the lore of some of  the new weapons and gear being  introduced in title update 15.  much like the existing named and exotic  items i haven't found everything or  figured out what they mean and some  don't have anything at all but for now  we'll be covering the catharsis exotic  mask king breaker named assault rifle  and deer named lmg  the catharsis is a new exotic mask being  introduced in title update 15. the  talent vicious cycle looks like an  interesting one that i can see myself  trying out on a tank build to provide  extra team support but this isn't what  i'm interested in here  if we look to the top there is a quote  that reads the establishment does  everything in its power to ensure that  the revolutionary rage is redirected  into empty outlets which provide  pressure releases for desires that could  become dangerous if allowed to progress  going back to the talent there is a  direct relation here where if i sum it  up in its most simple form the more  damage you take the more stacks and  power you obtain when a limit is reached  a cloud of healing is released purging  all status effects restoring armor to  you and those around you  this quote actually originates from a  book written by george l jackson called  blood in my eye  jackson was an american activist of  unbridled depression and racism  even while behind bars he was involved  in revolutionary activity taking a stand  at a time where the system was doing all  that it could to break his spirit  blood in my eye ties together a  collection of jackson's letters and  essays in which he presents his analysis  of armed struggle class war fascism  communism and a wide range of other  topics  it was completed only days before  jackson was killed by prison guards in  1971 during an alleged escape attempt  the quote used on the catharsis is only  a snippet of a much larger quote  fascism has established itself in a most  disguised and efficient manner in this  country it feels so secure that the  leaders allow us the luxury of a faint  protest  take the protests too far however and  they will show their other face  doors will be kicked down in the night  and machine gun fire and buckshot will  become the medium of exchange  the establishment does everything in its  power to ensure that revolutionary rage  is redirected into empty outlets which  provide pressure releases for desires  that could become dangerous if allowed  to progress  one has to understand that the fascist  arrangement tolerates the existence of  no valid revolutionary activity it is  programmed into its very nature a  massive complex and automatic defense  mechanism for all of our old methods for  raising the consciousness of a  potentially revolutionary class of  people  the essence of a usa totalitarian social  political capitalism is concealed behind  the illusion of a mass-participatory  society  we must rip away its mask then the  debate can end and we can enter a new  phase of struggle based on the  development of an armed revolutionary  culture that will triumph  this certainly sounds familiar when  referring to the division story but more  on this later  the king breaker is a new named assault  rifle as per all named items it provides  the perfect or fully optimized version  of a talent available on other items  in this case it's flatline with a  perfect version of his 20 amplified  weapon damage to pulsed enemies and  after two kills pulse is applied to the  next enemy that is hit  the quote on kingbreaker is the limits  of tyrants are prescribed by the  endurance of those whom they oppress  while i don't see any obvious relation  to the talent this quote comes from an  individual named frederick douglass  douglas was born in 1817 and after  escaping from slavery he would become  the leading african-american voice of  the 19th century  although douglas has been called the  father of the civil rights movement he  also assisted in shaping the american  nation as a woman's right activist  public speaker author journalist  publisher and social reformer  committed to freedom douglas dedicated  his life to achieving justice for all  americans in particular african  americans women and minority groups  he envisioned america as an inclusive  nation strengthened by diversity and  free of discrimination  douglas also served as an advisor to  presidents where abraham lincoln would  refer to him as the most meritorious man  of the 19th century  analyzing the quote on the king's lair  this could be considered a direct call  to action and while at the time this was  considered as a reference to slavery  there are many other issues douglas  supplied the same statement to  this is a warning not to accept make jew  and suffer tyranny lightly that by doing  so we put our own freedom at risk of  being harmed or destroyed  deer is a new name to lmg this is pretty  much the lmg version of the kingslayer  coming with the perfect flatline talent  along with a number of other items this  is showing that the developers are  looking to prop up the pulse skills  going forward these have perhaps been  underutilized across builds up until now  but this isn't the only similarity  across the two weapons  on the quote this weapon reads  if you dare to struggle you dare to win  if you dare not to struggle then damn it  you don't deserve to win  this follows the similar meaning behind  the king slayer quote where the message  is that you should fight for what you  believe in  much like the other two this quote comes  from american activist fred hampton  born in 1948 he would eventually become  the deputy chairman of the national  black panther party and chair of the  illinois chapter  hampton founded the anti-racist  anti-class rainbow coalition a prominent  multicultural political organization  that initially included the black  panthers young patriots poor whites and  the young lords hispanics and an  alliance among major chicago street  gangs to help end infighting and work  for social change  hampton considered fascism the greatest  threat  saying nothing is more important than  stopping fascism because fascism will  stop us all  he would eventually be killed in 1969 by  chicago police in a raid that saw more  than 90 bullets fired into the apartment  containing hampton his pregnant fiancee  and several other black panthers who  were sleeping  upon finding that hampton was still  alive he was executed by an officer at  close range who fired two bullets into  his head  while at this point it probably sounds  like i'm attempting to initiate some  sort of revolution i assure you that  this is not the case i'm waiting until i  have a much larger following before  going down that path but the origin of  these quotes all talk to similar aspects  fascist totalitarian and class-based  rule of which we have seen many examples  throughout history like benito mussolini  and adolf hitler and while ubisoft has  publicly stated in the past that their  games aren't political it can  understandably be a challenge to create  any sort of more grounded semi-realistic  good versus evil storyline without  intentionally or unintentionally having  some sort of association to events and  regimes that have happened in the past  or present  plus it doesn't help that people like  myself take enjoyment out of making  these sorts of games even more immersive  by attempting to close the gap between  fiction and reality  the division story has certainly been  leading us down a path of fascist  totalitarian and class-based rule with  the unknown employers behind natalia and  the black tusk attempting to gain  control over the united states of  america  but this is where i raised the question  to you  are these references simply just a nod  in the direction of prominent figures in  the american civil rights movement  or are these put in place to speak of  the similar and i use that word very  loosely situation that is playing out in  the division story  let me know what you think in the  comments  these are the type of topics that i love  coming across in games any excuse to  research real world history and attempt  to find ties within the story but as  always i could be completely over  analyzing something that has merely been  put into the game as just a powerful  thought-provoking quote to add some  filler in an area where perhaps no depth  was ever intended to be  placed anyway thank you very much for  watching and i'll catch in the next one  cheers  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]  foreign

